    "story": "Twenty minutes of ceremony behind them, and the whole rest of it ahead, and in between there is this: one aisle's worth of walking where they are married but nobody has thrown anything yet, congratulated them yet, fed them cake against their will yet. The bubbles were an aunt's idea, and a good one - they make the air itself look like it is applauding. Somebody's uncle is already thinking about the reception. They are thinking about nothing, gloriously, for the length of one walk. It is the last uncomplicated thirty feet of the day, and they are taking it at exactly the right speed.",
