    "story": "The show has no name on the building and no hour on the door, which is how the right people know they've found it. She does the gathering the old way: one raised hand, a voice pitched to carry exactly one street, and the promise - never spoken plainly - that what happens inside is not done anywhere else in this town. Half the crowd will swear later they decided to come in on their own. She lets them. A full house is a full house, and the first trick of the evening is always on the sidewalk.",
