    "story": "By daylight the whole act is exposed: a brick wall, a costume, a woman on an empty street tipping her hat to nobody in particular. That is the part the night audiences never understand - the character doesn't clock out. The bow is not for the camera. The bow is maintenance, the way a lighthouse keeps its own schedule whether or not a ship is watching. Somebody on this street will remember the hat tip at the exact moment they need to be braver about something. She won't be there to see it. That's how she'll know it worked.",
